-- §14  Supply that enters one total twice through two of a fusion's own parts, and no elimination for it.
# One row per supply that enters one total twice through two of a fusion's own parts, where the
# composer filed no elimination, beside the doubled layer's own demand and nameplate.
#
# The warning is the work
#   Not the structure. checks/jagged_layer.sqlc already reports that a fusion's parts overlap.
#   This asks the question a checker cannot: how much supply is in there twice, and did the
#   composer admit any of it. Where they did not, somebody downstream has to zero out an overlap
#   the filing left in, and the size of that job is filed nowhere. It is the pivot to the part
#   incidence, used as a measurement rather than as a correction: the doubled thing is a layer, so
#   it carries its own demand and nameplate, and the magnitude that would enter twice is readable
#   without anybody filing it.
#
# An admitted overlap is not this
#   `asrt:Elimination` is a composer finding the double counting and sizing it, which is the work
#   being done by the party who can actually see it. The `WHERE` here keeps only the fusions where
#   no elimination was filed at all, so a filing that did its own cleanup never appears, however
#   large its overlap was.
#
# Reading an empty result
#   Empty is the good outcome, and it is also what an unreached relation returns. This prints
#   nothing on a clean corpus. checks/jagged_layer.sqlc is what proves the question was asked.
-- composition/jagged_layers.sqlc for fusions with no filed elimination, against the doubled layer's own figures.
SELECT j.filing                                   AS "filing!",
       j.layer                                    AS "layer!",
       j.doubled_filing || '/' || j.doubled_layer AS "doubled!",
       j.via_layer                                AS "via!",
       j.also_via_layer                           AS "also_via!",
       f.d_mode::float8                           AS "twice_demand",
       f.n_mode::float8                           AS "twice_nameplate",
       coalesce(f.d_unit, f.n_unit, '')           AS "unit!"
FROM      (
    :compose(composition/jagged_layers.sqlc)
) j
LEFT JOIN (
    :compose(eliminations/filed.sqlc)
) e ON e.composition = j.filing AND e.composed_layer = j.layer
LEFT JOIN (
    :compose(layers/figures.sqlc)
) f ON f.filing = j.doubled_filing AND f.layer = j.doubled_layer
WHERE e.composition IS NULL
ORDER BY j.filing, j.layer, j.doubled_filing, j.doubled_layer
